{
  "description": "This protocol represents one of several protocols that prepares a panel of set dilutions of primary antibodies and fluorophores. This protocol creates Panel 1. The following antibodies and fluorophores dilutions are prepared in this panel:\nAntibodies\n CD4\n CD8\n FOXP3\n PD-L1 EL13N\n PAN CK\n KI-67\nFluorophores\n 520\n 570\n 540\n 620\n 650\n 690\n\n\nTo purchase tips, reagents, or pipettes, please visit our online store or contact our sales team at info@opentrons.com\n\nOpentrons OT-2\nOpentrons OT-2 Run App (Version 3.15.0 or later)\nOpentrons P10 Single-Channel Pipette\nOpentrons P1000 Single-Channel Pipette\nOpentrons 10µL Tips\nOpentrons 1000µL Tips\nCustom Tube Holder for 6mL Tubes and Tubes\nBio-Rad 96 Well Plate\nOpentrons 4-in-1 Tube Rack\nOpentrons 4-in-1 Tube Rack\n50mL Tubes\n2mL Tubes\n15mL Tubes\nAntibodies\nFluorophores\n\n\n\nSlot 1: Opentrons 1000µL Tips\nSlot 2: Custom 6mL Tube Rack Holder and Tubes\nSlot 3: Bio-Rad 96 Well Plate, for sample aliquots\nSlot 4: Opentrons 10µL Tips\nSlot 5: Opentrons 4-in-1 Tube Rack; 6x15mL, 4x50mL\n A3: Antibody Dilutent (initial volume=50mL)\n A4: Fluorophore Dilutent (initial volume=50mL)\nSlot 6: Opentrons 4-in-1 Tube Rack; 24x2mL\nSetup with initial volumes\n A1: 520, 75µL\n B1: 540, 75µL\n C1: 570, 75µL\n D1: 620, 75µL\n A2: 650, 75µL\n B2: 690, 75µL\n A3: CD3, 1000µL\n B3: CD4, 100µL\n C3: CD8, 100µL\n D3: CD20, 250µL\n A4: CD56, 1000µL\n B4: CD68, 100µL\n C4: CD163, 100µL\n D4: PD1, 100µL\n A5: PD-L1 EL13N, 100µL\n B5: FOXP3, 500µL\n C5: PAN CK, 1000µL\n D5: KI-67, 2000µL (Source 1)\n A6: KI-67, 2000µL (Source 2)\n B6: KI-67, 2000µL (Source 3)\n C6: KI-67, 2000µL (Source 4)\n D6: KI-67, 2000µL (Source 5)",
